From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d, d3d11: Direct3D 11.1 logic ops; D3D11_OPTIONS reports what is implemented

wined3d reports feature level 11_1 -- where Direct3D has the output-merger
logic ops -- but ignored a blend state's LogicOp ("Ignoring logic op") and
wrote the shader's colour as COPY does, and CheckFeatureSupport
(D3D11_OPTIONS) returned "fake" data with OutputMergerLogicOp FALSE.

The blend state now carries Direct3D 11.1's logic op (one for every render
target, from RenderTarget[0]); OpenGL applies it with glLogicOp (core since
1.1; off for blits and for independent blending), Vulkan with the
pipeline's logicOp where the device has the feature. As Direct3D does,
CreateBlendState1 refuses a logic op with IndependentBlendEnable. OPTIONS
reports what is implemented: the logic op from the device caps, ClearView
(render target and unordered access views, whole or by rectangles); the
rest stays FALSE because it is not done (ForcedSampleCount, discards and
copy flags reaching wined3d, msad4, extended doubles). Wine's own
test_logic_op now runs (it skipped) and passes.

Gate: test/d3d11logicop-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_NO_LOGIC_OP).
